_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 26
---
order: 26
---
short_label: XI.26
---
statement: To construct a solid angle equal to a given solid angle on a given straight line at a given point on it.
---
red_highlight: yes
---
proof:

Let *A* be the given point on the given straight line *AB,* and let the angle at *D* be the given solid angle contained by the angles *EDC, EDF,* and *FDC.*

It is required to construct at the point *A* on the straight line *AB* a solid angle equal to the solid angle at *D.*

Take a point *F* at random on *DF,* draw *FG* from *F* perpendicular to the plane through *ED* and *DC,* and let it meet the plane at *G.* Join *DG.* [!just XI.11]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="360" height="320" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XI.26 diagram" src="propXI26.gif"/></noscript>
